Use the Dutch National Flag Algorithm when the array contains only 3 unique values like 0, 1, and 2.


This algorithm is useful when the problem asks for:


sorting in one pass


O(n) time complexity


O(1) extra space


in-place sorting without using another array




The idea is to divide the array into 3 parts:


left side for 0s


middle for 1s


right side for 2s




We use three pointers:


low → position for next 0


mid → current element


high → position for next 2




While traversing:


if element is 0, swap with low


if element is 1, move ahead


if element is 2, swap with high




This algorithm is called the Dutch National Flag Algorithm because it partitions elements into three groups similar to the three colors of the Dutch flag.


Common interview problems using this approach:


Sort Colors


Sort 0s, 1s, and 2s


Three-way partitioning problems



